    "question": "Kendra has 4 packs of pens. Tony has 2 packs of pens. There are 3 pens in each pack. If Kendra and Tony decide to keep two pens each and give the remaining pens to their friends one pen per friend, how many friends will they give pens to?",
    "gold": "14",
    "answer": "Kendra has 4 packs x 3 pens/pack =<<4*3=12>>12 pens\nTony has 2 packs x 3 pens/pack = <<2*3=6>>6 pens\nIn total Kendra and Tony have 12 pens + 6 pens = <<12+6=18>>18 pens\nIf they each keep 2 pens, they keep 2 x 2 = <<2*2=4>>4 pens\nThey will be able to give a pen to 18 pens - 4 pens = <<18-4=14>>14 of their friends\n#### 14"
  },
  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many friends Kendra and Tony will give pens to, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Calculate the total number of pens Kendra has.\n2. Calculate the total number of pens Tony has.\n3. Determine how many pens Kendra and Tony will keep for themselves.\n4. Subtract the number of pens they keep from the total number of pens to find out how many pens they will give to their friends.\n5. Determine how many friends they will give pens to.\n\nLet's start with the first step:\n\n1. Kendra has 4 packs of pens, and each pack contains 3 pens. So, the total number of pens Kendra has is:\n   \\[\n   4 \\times 3 = 12\n   \\]\n\n2. Tony has 2 packs of pens, and each pack contains 3 pens. So, the total number of pens Tony has is:\n   \\[\n   2 \\times 3 = 6\n   \\]\n\n3. Kendra and Tony decide to keep 2 pens each. So, the total number of pens they keep is:\n   \\[\n   2 + 2 = 4\n   \\]\n\n4. The total number of pens they have together is:\n   \\[\n   12 + 6 = 18\n   \\]\n   After they keep 4 pens for themselves, the number of pens they will give to their friends is:\n   \\[\n   18 - 4 = 14\n   \\]\n\n5. Since they give one pen per friend, the number of friends they will give pens to is:\n   \\[\n   14\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the number of friends Kendra and Tony will give pens to is \\(\\boxed{14}\\).",
